title: "Sentinel: Stateless MCP Middleware for Identity-Aware RAG"
abstract: >
  Sentinel is a Model Context Protocol (MCP) server implementing
  Attribute-Based Access Control (ABAC) as middleware for RAG pipelines.
  It enforces zero-trust, fail-closed access control by performing a
  real-time Permission Handshake between the LLM and the knowledge base,
  inspired by the ReBAC principles of Google's Zanzibar system.
date-released: "2026-03-22"
